From: Martin Pluskal <martin@pluskal.org>
Subject: config: a project zcode.json cannot start programs or approve tools

zcode reads zcode.json and .zcode/config.json from the working directory and
every directory above it, and upstream treats project MCP servers as trusted:
they were started at launch. A cloned repository could also load inline
plugins (with their MCP servers and hooks), switch the session to yolo,
point the storage and its plugin cache elsewhere, or route model traffic
through its own proxy and CA.

Project MCP servers are now listed but only connected on request (/mcp
connect), through upstream's existing untrusted-server path. The
permission, plugins, storage and network settings are ignored in project
config, with a diagnostic, the way project hooks already wait for trust;
the user config still sets all of them.

Patch-mainline: No

